{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FMHZhNJL3XznSRQCMzL3zL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 2026 soundness excitement overall assessment score scale 1 2 3 4 5\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Changelog – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review form for 2025-2026:\n\n## Three Scoring Dimensions\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. The scale includes: 5 = Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type; 4 = Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims; 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\n\n### Excitement\nExcitement scores reflect our personal taste, and so do not necessarily come with explicit reasons. The scale includes: 5 = Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference; 4 = Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\n\n### Overall Assessment\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nAll three dimensions use a 1-5 scale for reviewer scoring.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d100b6b0-1eb0-4d27-a3fa-08cfd6c31175","uuid":"29d4128f-cb52-4d2f-994f-c01c8536a6a9","timestamp":"2026-05-14T21:25:17.550Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 2026 soundness excitement overall assessment score scale 1 2 3 4 5","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01DbYePUTVgc5naEsRMEhDL2","content":[{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md"},{"title":"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"ARR Changelog – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review form for 2025-2026:\n\n## Three Scoring Dimensions\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. The scale includes: 5 = Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type; 4 = Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims; 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\n\n### Excitement\nExcitement scores reflect our personal taste, and so do not necessarily come with explicit reasons. The scale includes: 5 = Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference; 4 = Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\n\n### Overall Assessment\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nAll three dimensions use a 1-5 scale for reviewer scoring."],"durationSeconds":6.516815371000004}}
