 to structurally simpler IE constraints\n- W2 (Major): Decidability taxonomy limited conceptual depth — follows directly from autoregressive generation properties\n- W3 (Moderate): CRANE cited but not empirically compared\n- W4 (Moderate): Missing connections to neuro-symbolic, structured prediction, constraint relaxation literature\n- W5 (Moderate): \"Enabling dependency\" inflated — architecturally self-evident\n- W6 (Minor): No engagement with type systems in NLP beyond code generation\n- W7 (Minor): \"First systematic study\" claim should be scoped more carefully\n\n**R2's key questions:**\n- Q1: What distinguishes OntoCoDec from PLDI'25 applied to simpler constraints?\n- Q2: How does OntoCoDec differ from EnriCo (ASP constraints during decoding)?\n- Q3: What happens when model generates entity in relation not in entity list?\n- Q4: Do violation landscape findings generalize beyond zero-shot?\n- Q5: How sensitive is tightness to observed vs. Cartesian type pairs?\n\n---\n\n## Your Task\n\nRead R2's review and respond with:\n\n1. **Points of agreement** with R2 (where R2 raised issues that align with or strengthen your concerns)\n2. **Points of disagreement** with R2 (where you think R2 is being too harsh or too lenient, and why)\n3. **New insights** from R2's review that change or refine your assessment\n4. **Would you revise your scores?** If so, how and why?\n\nKeep your response focused and under 600 words."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0188wWgjhsMVHvgkGEqUmG8A","session_id":"d100b6b0-1eb0-4d27-a3fa-08cfd6c31175","uuid":"09412845-f399-44c5-84c7-97142eb2a1aa","timestamp":"2026-05-14T21:29:51.345Z"}
